---

# 32. Failure Handling

An individual agent failure MUST NOT automatically crash the entire system.

Example:

```text
Retrieval Agent
      ↓
    FAILED
      ↓
Orchestrator
      ↓
Fallback
      ↓
Continue with reduced context
```

The failure should be recorded.

The final answer should indicate limitations when they materially affect reliability.

---

# 33. Agent Timeout

Each agent execution should have a configurable timeout.

Example:

```text
AGENT_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=30
```

A timed-out agent should return:

```text
status = failed
```

The workflow controller decides whether to:

* retry
* skip
* use fallback
* terminate

---

# 34. No Infinite Self-Improvement

The system MUST NOT continuously call itself to improve without a user task.

Every self-improvement cycle must originate from an actual task execution or an explicit developer test.

The system MUST NOT:

```text
learn
→ improve
→ execute
→ learn
→ improve
→ execute
```

forever.

---

# 35. No Source-Code Self-Modification

Phase 5 MUST NOT automatically modify:

* Python source code
* Agent source code
* Prompts
* Strategy implementation
* Workflow implementation
* Database schema
* Docker configuration
* Deployment configuration

The system learns through persistent data.

Source-code modification is explicitly out of scope.

